---
import { Image } from "astro:assets"
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro"
import corsImg from "@/assets/cors.jpg"
import gsocImg from "@/assets/gsoc.jpg"
import "@/styles/pages/articles.scss"
---

<Layout title="Articles | Oshan Mudannayake" description="Long-form technical articles by Oshan Mudannayake.">
    <div class="articlesLayout section-wrapper">
        <div class="section-title">
            <h1>Articles</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="section-items">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <div class="articles-card">
                        <div class="img-container cors">
                            <Image src={corsImg} alt="CORS" class="article-img" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-content">
                            <h3>CORS with WSO2 Identity Server 5.11</h3>
                            <span class="tags-text">wso2 identity server, cors</span><br />
                            <span class="content-text">
                                If you are here, chances are you know what CORS is. But let&rsquo;s go through the
                                basics in case you are a bit rusty on the exact way that CORS works. You can hop over to
                                the next section if you feel confident...{" "}
                                <a
                                    class="link"
                                    href="https://ivantha.medium.com/cors-with-wso2-identity-server-5-11-1067b3a6f9bd"
                                    target="_blank"
                                    rel="noopener noreferrer">[Read more]</a
                                >
                            </span><br />
                            <span class="date-text">Dec 4, 2020</span><br />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="articles-card">
                        <div class="img-container gsoc">
                            <Image src={gsocImg} alt="GSoC" class="article-img" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-content">
                            <h3>GSoC diaries I - Long walk to GSoC with CERN-HSF</h3>
                            <span class="tags-text">open source, gsoc, cern, owncloud</span><br />
                            <span class="content-text">
                                Google Summer of Code is an annual initiative carried out by Google for the betterment
                                of the open-source software and the students in STEM fields. It started in 2005 as a
                                program that would help students...{" "}
                                <a
                                    class="link"
                                    href="https://ivantha.medium.com/gsoc-diaries-part-i-long-walk-to-gsoc-with-cern-hsf-92e671fad4f5"
                                    target="_blank"
                                    rel="noopener noreferrer">[Read more]</a
                                >
                            </span><br />
                            <span class="date-text">Nov 18, 2019</span><br />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
